  "id": "stuttering",
  "term": "stuttering",
  "definition": "Stuttering is a speech fluency disturbance in which the timing and flow of speech are not typical for the person’s age. It commonly involves repeated or prolonged sounds or syllables, and can also include blocks, broken words, extra tension during speech, and other dysfluencies; it may begin in childhood or be acquired in association with brain disease.",
